+  "problem_number": "OWR-17469-011",
+  "title": "Large Deviations for Random High-Dimensional Projections",
+  "statement": "Let $\\Theta^{(N)}$ be uniform on $S^{N-1}$ and set $\\nu_N=\\mu_{\\Theta^{(N)}}$. Does $(\\nu_N)$ satisfy a large-deviation principle with speed $N$ and rate function\n\n$$I(\\nu)=-\\frac12\\log(1-\\|\\alpha\\|_2^2)$$\n\nwhen $\\nu=\\kappa_\\alpha$ for some $\\alpha$ in the open unit ball of $\\ell_2$, and $I(\\nu)=\\infty$ otherwise? As an intermediate step, are the possible Prohorov limits of\n\n$$E_N=\\left\\{\\operatorname{law}\\!\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^N\\alpha_iU_i\\right):\\alpha\\in S^{N-1}\\right\\}$$\n\nexactly $\\{\\kappa_\\alpha:\\alpha\\in\\ell_2,\\ \\|\\alpha\\|_2\\leq1\\}$?",
+  "background": "Collected from Oberwolfach Reports, which document mathematical workshops and their open-problem discussions.\n\n**Source report:** [New Perspectives and Computational Challenges in High Dimensions (2021), Oberwolfach Reports, DOI 10.4171/owr/2020/6, pp. 377--416](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2020/6)\n\n## Literature review (checked 2026-08-22)\n\n**Status:** open\n\n**Assessment.** The 2021 report states this large-deviation principle and its compactness lemma as conjectural; the checked literature gives no proof of the full claim by 2026-08-22.\n\n**Sources checked.**\n\n- [Oberwolfach report on the conjecture](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2020/6)\n\nThis is a dated literature triage derived from the supplied OWR curation; verify time-sensitive status and cited claims independently.",
