+  "original_statement": "Conjecture: if Theta^(N) is uniform on the unit sphere S^(N-1) and nu-N=mu-Theta^(N), then (nu-N) satisfies a large deviation principle with rate N and rate function I(nu)=-1/2 log(1-||alpha||^2) when nu=kappa-alpha for some alpha in the unit ball of l-2 with ||alpha||<1, and I(nu)=infinity otherwise. A necessary intermediate claim is that the possible Prohorov limits of laws in E-N={law(sum-subscript-i=1-to-N alpha-i U-i): alpha in S^(N-1)} are exactly {kappa-alpha: alpha in the unit ball of l-2}.",
+  "clean_statement": "Let $\\Theta^{(N)}$ be uniform on $S^{N-1}$ and set $\\nu_N=\\mu_{\\Theta^{(N)}}$. Does $(\\nu_N)$ satisfy a large-deviation principle with speed $N$ and rate function\n\n$$I(\\nu)=-\\frac12\\log(1-\\|\\alpha\\|_2^2)$$\n\nwhen $\\nu=\\kappa_\\alpha$ for some $\\alpha$ in the open unit ball of $\\ell_2$, and $I(\\nu)=\\infty$ otherwise? As an intermediate step, are the possible Prohorov limits of\n\n$$E_N=\\left\\{\\operatorname{law}\\!\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^N\\alpha_iU_i\\right):\\alpha\\in S^{N-1}\\right\\}$$\n\nexactly $\\{\\kappa_\\alpha:\\alpha\\in\\ell_2,\\ \\|\\alpha\\|_2\\leq1\\}$?",
